{
 "metadata": {
  "name": "EXP \u00b7 TEGOTAE \u00b7 bare load rule trots (sim, CAD body)",
  "description": "WATCH: the diagonal pairs (FL+RR, FR+RL) land together, a trot that no line of code names. Owaki & Ishiguro's rule alone (LoadPhaseGait, absolute foot load, sigma_r 1.75, period 70) drives the legs through the hip stroke (0.525, inside the 3.67 rad/s slew) and a swing lift (hip2 -0.6 / knee +0.4); every other joint writer is OFF (learned layer motor_gain 0, stance press, tuck, heading hold, level gate, noise, panic) and the GainEvolver is removed. Only the posture spring stays. Expect drift and curving: there is no heading hold. Arena n=6 x 4500 (CAD body, 2 mm contact, 256 solver iterations \u2014 the sim defaults from 2026-10-19): 5.32 +/- 0.73 m, straight 0.82, 0 falls; corridor 4.45 +/- 1.64 m but 0.67 falls (no heading hold: it climbs the side walls). A MEASUREMENT SCAFFOLD (the phase-to-joint map stands in for Owaki's crank), not a brain to deploy. Compare against 'PROMOTED \u00b7 LPG stack (sim)': its oscillators trot, its feet do not (97 % irregular strides). Plan: docs/plans-and-designs/tegotae_replication_plan.md.",
